WEBVTT

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.080
Happy Birthday,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:09.490
Nao!

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.580
Lala!

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.270
Here's your present.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:12.990
Here's yours.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:13.660
Thanks!

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.910
I love celebrating our birthdays together.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.010
Yeah!

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.930
Um, so...

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.210
The perfect idol pattern...

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.200
It's gotta be lovely...

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.100
Kano-pero!

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.710
pop...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:30.510
Pipi!

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.220
and cool...

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.170
Ju.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.390
If I matched them to Pepper and Chiri...

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.640
You want to eat too?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.420
You there, prostrate yourself and capisce!

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.820
No way, no way, no way!

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.760
There's no way it'll work!

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.010
I don't know what to do with NonSugar at all...

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.130
Non!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:55.340
Lala's going to be back any minute! Time for one last rehearsal!

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.610
Oh, right! Today's Onee-chan's birthday!

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:03.180
And I've been so busy thinking about NonSugar that I forgot to get her a present!

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.000
Oh no, what do I do?

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.220
I'm back!

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.430
Hm? Hey, Dad! Mum! Non!

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.900
Surprise!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.610
Congra-trattoria on your special day!

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.810
Thanks so much, you guys!

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.020
And now a toast to the lady of the hour:

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.990
Cheers!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:06.700
Japanese
Dictionary

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.420
This present's from me, Lala.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.250
Train your idol power <i>and</i> brainpower.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.170
A dictionary... uh, thank you!

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.370
I got you this.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.480
They say it's more popular than carved bears in the Sapanna.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.680
A wood carving of a shoebill catching a catfish?

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.850
Uh... thank you! I'll treasure it forever.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.020
Lala.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.650
Your present from your father and me is this:

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:37.390
Signore, signora, signorina!

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.220
It's time for the SoLaMi SMILE live show!

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.620
Hi, everyone! Lala here!

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.820
She said she's twelve years old.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:49.530
By the way, did you know the common jellyfish lives to six months of age?

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.860
Lala, Happ-pri Birthday!

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.260
It's amazingly bad. Especially Lala.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.720
How lovely!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:09.900
Oh yeah!

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:10.910
This is pretty good!

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.060
I love it!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.320
Yay!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.490
Capisce!

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.960
Mum and dad's birthday present...

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.630
was this SoLaMi SMILE performance!

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:28.030
And we were one short, so we got Non to lend us her assis-salami pizza!

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.350
Thank you very much! It made me really happy!

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.540
Thank you too, Non.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.620
Um, I was just helping out...

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:42.250
About <i>my</i> present... I hadn't really decided what I should get you...

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.240
Onee-chan, is there something you...

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.760
Don't worry about it! I'm super happy you put on this show for me!

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:53.300
I know I'd be really happy if I cotta sister duet!

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.520
Oh, yes! When you were in kindergarten, you'd put on little shows all the time!

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.530
Hey, you're right...

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.760
The two of us were always singing together...

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.220
and we promised we'd perform as sisters when our PriTickets arrived.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:14.120
Non! There's a present I want after all!

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.220
Didn't you just say not to worry about it?

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.900
I changed my mind!

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:24.380
Non! For my present, I want to do a birthday performance with you in PriPara!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.680
What? I can't do that!

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.310
Onee-chan, you're my <i>rival</i> right now! My nemesis!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:36.780
Oh, come on! It's just for today,
and it's my birthday,you know... okay?

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.760
And you promised back then! Okay? Okay? Okay?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:40.820
Like I said...

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.770
No means no!

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.190
Non!

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.850
Are you kidding me?

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:51.300
I need to concentrate on NonSugar right now.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.660
As if I could do a birthday performance with my nemesis...

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.300
And I don't even want to hear the word "birthday"...

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:05.160
<i>This "birthday party" event will be an excellent opportunity to develop your bond as teammates.</i>

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:06.360
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.090
<i>You three members of NonSugar
shall hold the event, come what may!</i>

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.480
<i>Good heavens, this "party" is a drab affair.</i>

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.520
<i>Eh? Well, we all pitched in, since it's your birthday...</i>

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.660
<i>I don't recall asking you to "pitch in"!</i>

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.670
<i>Ooh-ooh!</i>

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.610
<i>You want to eat too?</i>

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:28.630
<i>Chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan-shan!</i>

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.250
<i>Pepper! No eating with your hands!</i>

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.600
<i>I taught you how to use a knife and fork, remember?</i>

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.080
<i>Let the filth be banished!</i>

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:35.230
<i>Be cleansed! Be cleansed! Be cleansed!</i>

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.620
<i>Purr, purr!</i>

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.500
<i>I brought some drinks-uch–</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.330
<i>Be cleansed! Be cleansed! Be cleansed!</i>

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:39.760
<i>Chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan, chiri-shan-shan! Filth! Filth! Unconscionable filth!</i>

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.550
<i>Would you cut it out?</i>

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.100
<i>It's hard for me to handle gross stuff, too, you know!</i>

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.300
<i>I can't take this anymore!</i>

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:52.010
Why can't we be a team like Onee-chan's?

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.560
How is Onee-chan different to me?

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.980
Non!

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.000
Are you ready to perform with me yet?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:01.940
Well, are you?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.090
I'm not in the mood for this.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.820
Okay, this time we're gonna bond our butts off!

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.700
Aw... should I give up on my sisterly birthday performance?

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.320
Mama!

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.850
No-no! No-no! Ma-ma...

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.700
Hey, Jululu. Do you want to see us together, too?

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:32.670
Leave it to me, Jululu! I'll travel east to west, west to east,

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:35.080
to the Sapanna, the Norp Pole – wherever it takes!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.670
No matter what happens, we'll put on that sister show!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.150
Ta-da!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.080
Found ya, Non!

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.460
Onee-chan!

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.280
I <i>thought</i> it was weird that you left before me.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.760
You were waiting for me...

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.140
Come on, Non, let's do a show together! Okay?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.410
I told you! I'm not in the mood!

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:07.590
You're not getting away <i>that</i> easily, my dear.
Your onee-chan's not gonna give up.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.850
Non!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.710
More importantly, what should I do about NonSugar?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.480
Article 235 of Paprika Academy regulations:

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:25.770
no sighing in the courtyard!

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.610
No sighing in
the courtyard

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.860
Head Disciplinarian Minami...

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.920
If you sigh, your happiness will escape you.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.940
You can talk to me if you'd like.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:39.580
Actually, Head Disciplinarian Minami...

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.440
Aw, Non ran away from me again...

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.660
What do I have to do to get her to perform with me?

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:51.780
You can't always get your feelings across in Ren-words, my dear.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.050
Ajimi-sensei!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.340
The best way to do it...

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:58.490
is to slam your feelings into them-Da Vinci!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.720
Allow Ponkan to share her expertise on reaching another's heart:

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.940
the fruit of her many years of experience slamming her feelings into othe-Ruvens!

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.520
Please do, Maestro Da Vinci!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:16.620
I see, so you're lost on how to
properly unite the team you've just formed.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:21.790
Um, how was it when SoLaMi SMILE first formed?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.720
Good question.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:27.250
Back then, you could say I was pretty desperate.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.250
I hadn't been able to form a team at all.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:39.120
I even went so far as to deliberately drop my PriTicket bag trying to find a teammate.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.400
What? You dropped your bag <i>deliberately</i>?

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.140
I did.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.980
I figured if a kind-hearted girl went all the way to bring it to me,

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.810
there'd be no way she could refuse to sing with me, too.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.220
It was all part of my calculated plan.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.880
C–Calculated?

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.070
Back then, I would have taken <i>anyone</i> as a teammate.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:03.630
<i>Pri-please!</i>

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:08.370
<i>I've been training so hard for this audition – day in, day out!</i>

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.630
<i>Pri-please help me out! I'm begging you-pri!</i>

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.630
<i>But I've never sung on stage!</i>

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.710
<i>I've never danced either.</i>

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.880
<i>But do you like PriPara?</i>

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.840
<i>I love it!</i>

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.350
<i>Then you'll be fine! I'm pri-sure you can do it!</i>

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.140
<i>Please?</i>

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.220
<i>Capisce!</i>

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.780
But you know what? Then I heard her sing,
and that's when I knew for sure.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:30.770
"It's this girl or no one."

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:37.260
When she was afraid of flouting the school's PriPara ban,

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.240
she'd end up not being able to come to our shows.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.000
<i>I'm not giving up-pri!</i>

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.700
<i>Easy to say, but-kuma...</i>

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.180
<i>We promised-pri.</i>

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.210
I believed she'd come, no matter what.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.580
Why did you trust her so much?

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:57.130
Her eyes. I could tell from her eyes she'd never lie to me.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.650
That's how I knew.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.970
<i>I... really wanted to sing with you again.</i>

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.730
I haven't thought about that in a long time.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:09.970
So SoLaMi SMILE had it tough at first, too...

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.580
I was pretty obstinate myself,

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:16.040
but you should have seen the lengths Lala went to.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.980
Onee-chan too?

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:21.890
That's right. Especially when she wanted to get Sophie to join our team –

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.990
she really dug in her heels.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:28.250
<i>"Don't say </i>can't <i>! because you can! You can! You can! I know you can!",</i>

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.960
<i>... they said.</i>

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:32.500
<i>Are you really okay with this?</i>

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:36.090
<i>You saw how much Sophie-san wants out!</i>

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.920
<i>I know you're actually bothered by it!</i>

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.850
Onee-chan said all that?

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:45.640
She did. You'll have to ask Sophie herself for the full story.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.230
Found ya, Non!

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.610
Let's do a show!

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:54.490
I know I just said it, but you really do
<i>slam</i> your feelings across.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.520
That said...

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.840
Article 391 of Paprika Academy regulations:

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:00.400
"No climbing the statue of the school founder"!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:02.570
Capisce!

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:11.470
Non, let's do a show!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.170
For the last time, I'm not in the mood!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:18.340
Ajimi-sensei! I did it just like you said, but it didn't work!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.280
Well, then.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.380
"Go some distance away because then the work appears smaller

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.380
and more of it can be taken in at a glance and a lack of harmony and proportion is more readily seen."

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:28.550
Thus spoke Leonardo da Vinci.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:29.530
La-dee-dah-, dah, dah...

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.430
"Go some distance away"?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:32.560
Ta-dah!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.680
And what's further away than space-Da Vinci?

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.400
Slip the surly Bosch of earth and soar
beyond the atmosph-Hieronymus:

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.900
be brought to your knee-elsen by the glory of space, oh, Dupont!

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.110
Space...

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.140
If you have a pure heart, you can view-sseau it.

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:47.380
V-ewis, vie-byov, vie-che, vie-doute it!

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.410
There's nowhere we can't Gogh!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.580
Three, two, one: let's Gauguin!

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.040
Whu–

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.380
Sensei! Where are we?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.260
The cosmos!

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:19.460
Man, I'm <i>beat</i>...

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.080
Hey there.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:24.820
So I hear you wanna hear the story of how we formed a team?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:25.900
What?

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.700
I sure had it tough back then.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:33.770
Shion and Reona didn't get along at all, you see, and were always bickering.

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.960
That's when <i>I</i> had to step in as the voice of–

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.680
Having an active imagination is one thing,

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.250
but this bears no relation to the truth.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:44.470
A pack of lies – no, an hundred packs of lies.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.300
U–Um, so anyway...

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.570
The first time I met Lala...

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.430
S-Sophie-san?

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:55.970
... was in the entrance to my apartment.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:02.110
I ordered Red Flash pizzas and Lala came to deliver them.

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:05.030
So you met when she delivered fast food to you?

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:09.370
That they did. Back then, we were guarding Sophie day and night –

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:13.040
there's no other way she could have got near her.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:17.790
But Lala would charge through our
iron defences time and time again-chanko.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.290
Lala, stand and Renaiss-hold!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.000
Ooh!

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.460
So that's the Mil-something Way...

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.440
Say, isn't that blue dot in the distance...

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.260
It's the Earth-Da Vinci!

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.380
From this vantage point,
Earth, Jupiter and Saturn are but specks!

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:36.180
Simple trash-Da Vinci!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.040
I see!

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:44.260
From here, the whole world looks tiny,
and Parajuku is even tinier!

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:48.530
And my worries are even tinier again!

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.820
Indeed: "the eye is the window of the soul"!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.300
Thus spoke Leonardo da Vinci.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.040
I think I get it, Ajimi-sensei!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:02.270
Compared to all of space,
I'm as small and insignificant as eye mucus!

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.420
But my desire to perform with Non

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.660
is as big as this whole Mil-something Way!

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:10.380
I'll take that desire and hit my little sister with it–

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:15.470
Th–This is bad-Da Vinci!
There's a meteor incoming-Da Vinci!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.250
Time to depart-chenko!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.610
It's the Glo Comet!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.820
You must not run in the hallways!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.990
We must break th-Ruvens!

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:36.200
I believe I said you mustn't run! Are you listening?

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:40.660
We'll make it back to Earth, Ajimi-sensei – I know it!

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:40.960
Aye!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.670
Wee-woo!

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:47.950
When Sophie was agonising over
joining a team with New and Mew, too...

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:53.640
Lala helped us figure out what would really make Sophie happy-chanko!

